title: Settings › Agents › What each freedom level allows and the gates it never skips
route: /settings
intro: The three levels set how much an agent does before a person looks. Five gates sit above every level. The page names the levels, says in one line what each changes (the 'What each level changes' card) and shows the Gates card. The PRD guardrail matrix gives the wider meaning.
dir: TD
also: The mapping from the three demo labels to the PRD words (Stage or Draft, Auto + notify, Auto) is our reading. The PRD sets autonomy per action, not per agent. In the demo the levels are applied in EMR Connect only.
---
start s1 "An agent is about to take a step"
decision q0 "Is it clinical content or a clinical decision?"
endx x1 "Never done by an agent at any level\nWriting or editing assessments, plans, diagnoses or scores\nChoosing units, frequency or dates\nAnswering a payer's clinical questions\nPausing, discharging or continuing a patient"
decision q1 "Is the step one of the five gates?"
decision q3 "Which level is set on the agent's row?"

group gGate "The five gates (the Gates card), above every level"
  click g1 "Sign-off\nA licensed clinician signs every request and appeal"
  click g2 "Confirm\nThe case owner confirms before agents start, before a next step on a denial, and before any write-back"
  input g3 "Answer\nA person answers when an agent asks a question"
  click g4 "Acknowledge\nA person acknowledges a payer rule change before drafts are updated"
  click g5 "Pause\nAn operator can pause one agent or all of them"
endgroup

group gLev "The three levels (Freedom dropdown)"
  process l1 "Ask before acting\nOn the page: 'Waits for your OK. Reader asks before it syncs, and Navigator before it fixes or reconnects a system.'\n(PRD: Stage or Draft)"
  process l2 "Act, then report\nOn the page: 'Goes ahead, then reports what it did in a toast and in Recent activity.'\n(PRD: Auto + notify)"
  process l3 "Act on its own\nOn the page: 'Goes ahead and only logs what it did in Recent activity, with no toast.'\n(PRD: Auto)"
endgroup

process p1 "The signature is bound to the exact packet\nNothing addressed to a payer leaves without it. PRD: an invariant, not a setting"
process p2 "The step goes ahead"
goto n1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Review & submit › Sign and send to payer"
goto n2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Approve the write-back"
goto n3 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Authorization preparation › An agent asks a question"
goto n4 "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Acknowledge a change"
goto n5 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause all agents"
goto n6 "Continues in: Settings › Agents › Which steps need a person"
goto n7 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › When an agent is paused or asks first"

s1 --> q0
q0 -->|Yes| x1
q0 -->|No| q1
q1 -->|Yes| g1 & g2 & g3 & g4 & g5
q1 -->|No| q3
q3 -->|Ask before acting| l1
q3 -->|Act, then report| l2
q3 -->|Act on its own| l3
g1 --> p1 --> p2
g2 --> p2
g3 --> p2
g4 --> p2
g5 --> p2
l1 --> p2
l2 --> p2
l3 --> p2
g1 -.-> n1
g2 -.-> n2
g3 -.-> n3
g4 -.-> n4
g5 -.-> n5
q3 -.-> n6
l1 -.-> n7
